  "output": "Good — all findings are verified. Here's the full performance analysis:\n\n---\n\n## Performance Analysis\n\n### 1. N+1 Query Patterns (High Severity)\n\n**`apps/api/src/server/plugins/realtime-plugin.ts`** — every mutation side-effect handler loops and fires individual `findUnique` calls per row.\n\n**Post handler (lines 63–89)**\n```typescript\n// BAD: N db.group.findUnique() calls inside loop\nfor (const post of rows) {\n  const group = await db.group.findUnique({ where: { id: groupId } })   // line 73\n  const mentioned = await mentionedReaders(str(post.content), groupId)  // line 78 — also queries inside\n}\n```\nFix — batch outside the loop:\n```typescript\nconst groupIds = [...new Set(rows.map(r => str(r.groupId)))]\nconst groups = await db.group.findMany({ where: { id: { in: groupIds } }, select: { id: true, organizationId: true } })\nconst groupMap = new Map(groups.map(g => [g.id, g]))\nfor (const post of rows) {\n  const group = groupMap.get(str(post.groupId))\n  // ...\n}\n```\n\n**Comment handler (lines 92–144)**: `db.post.findUnique()` at line 95 and `db.comment.findUnique()` at line 127 are called per comment row.\n\n**PostReaction handler (lines 146–188)**: `db.post.findUnique()` at line 149 + `db.notification.findFirst()` at line 166 both fire per reaction. The notification coalesce check is especially expensive.\n\n**CommentReaction handler (lines 191–205)**: Same pattern — `db.comment.findUnique()` per reaction at line 194.\n\nFix for reactions — batch post lookups and coalesce with one `findMany`:\n```typescript\nconst postIds = [...new Set(rows.map(r => str(r.postId)))]\nconst posts = await db.post.findMany({\n  where: { id: { in: postIds } },\n  select: { id: true, authorId: true, groupId: true, group: { select: { organizationId: true } } }\n})\nconst postMap = new Map(posts.map(p => [p.id, p]))\n\n// Batch the coalesce check\nconst existing = await db.notification.findMany({\n  where: { postId: { in: postIds }, type: \"POST_REACTION\", readAt: null },\n  select: { postId: true, actorId: true }\n})\nconst existingSet = new Set(existing.map(n => `${n.postId}:${n.actorId}`))\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Unnecessary React Re-renders (Medium Severity)\n\n**`apps/web/src/components/chat/message-list.tsx` line 81**\n```typescript\n// Runs on every render — creates two new arrays each time\nconst messages = data.pages.flat().reverse()\n```\nFix:\n```typescript\nconst messages = useMemo(() => data.pages.flat().reverse(), [data.pages])\n```\n\n**`apps/web/src/components/feed/post-feed.tsx` lines 93–96**\n```typescript\n// Runs on every render\nconst posts = [\n  ...(pinnedFirst ? (pinned.data ?? []) : []),\n  ...data.pages.flat(),\n]\n```\nFix:\n```typescript\nconst posts = useMemo(() => [\n  ...(pinnedFirst ? (pinned.data ?? []) : []),\n  ...data.pages.flat(),\n], [pinnedFirst, pinned.data, data.pages])\n```\n\n**`apps/web/src/components/chat/message-list.tsx` line 44** — `new Date()` called inside `dayLabel` during every render for year comparison. Since `dayLabel` is called per message group, this creates many `Date` objects. Use `useNow()` (already exists in the project) or hoist the year constant:\n```typescript\nconst currentYear = new Date().getFullYear()  // outside component, or via useNow()\n\nfunction dayLabel(d: Date, currentYear: number) {\n  if (isToday(d)) return \"Today\"\n  if (isYesterday(d)) return \"Yesterday\"\n  return format(d, d.getFullYear() === currentYear ? \"EEEE, MMMM d\" : \"MMMM d, yyyy\")\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. Memory Leaks (Medium Severity)\n\n**`apps/web/src/components/chat/composer.tsx` lines 85–90** — `requestAnimationFrame` id is not cancelled on unmount. If the component unmounts during the animation frame (e.g., navigation while typing), the callback still fires and tries to access `wrapperRef.current`:\n```typescript\n// BAD — no cleanup\nuseEffect(() => {\n  if (modeKey)\n    requestAnimationFrame(() =>\n      wrapperRef.current?.querySelector(\"textarea\")?.focus()\n    )\n}, [modeKey])\n```\nFix:\n```typescript\nuseEffect(() => {\n  if (!modeKey) return\n  const id = requestAnimationFrame(() =>\n    wrapperRef.current?.querySelector(\"textarea\")?.focus()\n  )\n  return () => cancelAnimationFrame(id)\n}, [modeKey])\n```\n\n**`apps/api/src/websocket/calls.ts` lines 234–237** — the ring timeout `setTimeout` is never cleared if the call is manually ended before it fires. It holds a reference to `call.id` and calls `endCall` unnecessarily (guarded by `live.has(call.id)`, so functionally safe, but leaks the timer handle):\n```typescript\n// Track timers so they can be cleared\nconst ringTimers = new Map<string, ReturnType<typeof setTimeout>>()\n\nconst timer = setTimeout(() => {\n  ringTimers.delete(call.id)\n  if (!answered.has(call.id) && live.has(call.id))\n    endCall(call.id).catch(logError(\"ring timeout\"))\n}, RING_TIMEOUT_MS)\nringTimers.set(call.id, timer)\n\n// In endCall, add:\nclearTimeout(ringTimers.get(callId))\nringTimers.delete(callId)\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. Caching Opportunities\n\n**`apps/web/src/lib/query.ts`** — `gcTime` is not set. The React Query default is 5 minutes, but being explicit and extending it reduces cold-cache refetches for stable data (org members, groups):\n```typescript\ndefaultOptions: {\n  queries: {\n    staleTime: 30_000,\n    gcTime: 10 * 60 * 1000,   // add this\n    refetchOnWindowFocus: false,\n  },\n}\n```\n\n**`apps/api/src/routes/files.ts` line ~24`** — presigned URLs expire in 5 minutes but the cache header is only 240s (4 min). Align them:\n```typescript\nset.headers[\"cache-control\"] = \"private, max-age=270\"  // 30s safety margin before 5m expiry\n```\n\n**`mentionedReaders` in `realtime-plugin.ts` lines 30–50`** — called once per post/comment in the handlers loop. It always re-fetches `db.group.findUnique` for the same group. After the batch refactor above, pass the already-fetched group object in directly to eliminate the inner query entirely:\n```typescript\nasync function mentionedReaders(text: string, groupId: string, group: { privacy: string, organizationId: string }) {\n  // remove the db.group.findUnique call — group is passed in\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 5. Redundant Computations\n\n**`apps/web/src/components/chat/message-list.tsx` line 82`** — `members.find()` runs on every render of `MessageList`. With small member counts this is trivial, but it should be:\n```typescript\nconst myMember = useMemo(() => members.find(m => m.userId === me.id), [members, me.id])\n```\n\n---\n\n### Summary by Impact\n\n| Issue | File | Lines | Impact |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| N+1: Comment loop queries | `realtime-plugin.ts` | 92–144 | **High** |\n| N+1: Reaction loop queries | `realtime-plugin.ts` | 146–205 | **High** |\n| N+1: Post loop queries | `realtime-plugin.ts` | 63–90 | **High** |\n| Memory: rAF not cancelled | `composer.tsx` | 85–90 | Medium |\n| Memory: ring timer not tracked | `calls.ts` | 234–237 | Low |\n| Re-render: messages array | `message-list.tsx` | 81–82 | Medium |\n| Re-render: posts array | `post-feed.tsx` | 93–96 | Medium |\n| Re-render: `new Date()` in dayLabel | `message-list.tsx` | 44 | Low |\n| Cache: missing gcTime | `query.ts` | 28 | Low |\n| Cache: presigned URL max-age | `files.ts` | ~24 | Low |\n\nThe highest-ROI fix is batching the N+1 queries in `realtime-plugin.ts` — every mutation currently fires O(rows) sequential DB round trips, and under load (bulk imports, broadcast reactions) this will bottleneck the entire mutation pipeline. The React fixes are easy wins but low latency impact given React Query's deduplication.\n",
